{"cuisine/shippoku":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/shippoku","n":"Shippoku","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Japanese Chinese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Japan","intro":[["Shippoku is a Japanese culinary style that is heavily influenced by Chinese cuisine. It has been described as a fusion cuisine and as a \"hybrid cuisine\" that combines elements of European, Chinese and Japanese cuisines. Meats used in shippoku cuisine include fowl, fish, and game meats. Sake typically accompanies shippoku dishes. The shippoku style of service typically includes several small dishes that comprise a full meal."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"shippoku"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shippoku"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Japanese Chinese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Japanese Chinese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"cuisine/azerbaijani-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/azerbaijani-cuisine","n":"Azerbaijani cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Caucasian cuisine","cuisine/caucasian-cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Azerbaijan","intro":[["Azerbaijani cuisine is a term describing the cooking styles and dishes of the Republic of Azerbaijan. The cuisine is influenced by the country's agriculture that mostly developed on grasslands allowing a culture of pastoralism to develop, as well as to the geographical location of the country, which is situated between Europe and Asia with access to the Caspian Sea. This location has enabled the people that now live in the territory of Azerbaijan to develop a diet rich in produce, milk products, and meat, including beef, mutton, fish and game. The location, which was contested by many historical kingdoms, khanates, and empires, also meant that Azerbaijani cuisine was influenced by the culinary traditions of multiple different cultures, including Turkic, Iranian, Armenian and Eastern European cuisines. Many dishes of Armenian cuisine and Georgian cuisine with Turkified or Turkic names are widespread in Azerbaijan."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"azerbaijani-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azerbaijani_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Caucasian cuisine","cuisine/caucasian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Pomegranates & Saffron: A Culinary Journey to Azerbaijan","ref":"cookbook/pomegranates-saffron-a-culinary-journey-to-azerbaijan","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Feride Buyuran, 2015","note":"Large collection of Azerbaijani recipes with cultural background.","url":"","suggested":true},{"name":"Kaukasis: A Culinary Journey through Georgia, Azerbaijan & Beyond","ref":"cookbook/kaukasis-a-culinary-journey-through-georgia-azerbaijan-beyond","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Olia Hercules, 2017","note":"Recipes gathered across the Caucasus, mostly Georgia and Azerbaijan.","url":"https://www.simonandschuster.ca/books/Kaukasis/Olia-Hercules/9781681883038","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":12,"links":[["Badambura","dish/badambura"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Doghramaj","dish/doghramaj"],["Dovga","dish/dovga"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Scorched rice","dish/scorched-rice"],["Shekerbura","dish/shekerbura"],["Sheki halva","dish/sheki-halva"],["Shorgoghal","dish/shorgoghal"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Syrup","ingredient/syrup"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Hazelnut","ingredient/hazelnut"],["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Ayran","ingredient/ayran"],["Dill","ingredient/dill"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Mentha","ingredient/mentha"],["Qatiq","ingredient/qatiq"],["Spinach","ingredient/spinach"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yogurt","ingredient/yogurt"],["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Rumen","ingredient/rumen"],["Animal fats and oils","ingredient/animal-fats-and-oils"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Dried fruit","ingredient/dried-fruit"],["Lard","ingredient/lard"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Caucasian cuisine","cuisine/caucasian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"cuisine/frisian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/frisian-cuisine","n":"Frisian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Germany","intro":[["Frisian cuisine consists of the traditional recipes and cooking methods of the historic region of Frisia, which is in present-day Germany and the Netherlands. Frisian cuisine is diverse, drawing from both land and sea. Most dishes, excluding desserts, are made of fish or potatoes, though there are several dishes based on other ingredients. Especially in West Frisia, the food resembles that of the Dutch Cuisine, though East Frisia and North Frisia present dishes that are very much unique to the region."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"frisian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frisian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine"},"dish/aan-de-poel":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/aan-de-poel","n":"Aan de Poel","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Aan de Poel is a fine-dining restaurant in Amstelveen, Netherlands that was awarded one Michelin star for the period 200