nha","dish/francesinha"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Carne-seca","ingredient/carne-seca"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Parsley","ingredient/parsley"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Beer","ingredient/beer"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Chipolata","ingredient/chipolata"],["Ham","ingredient/ham"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]}]},"dish/bear-paw":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bear-paw","n":"Bear paw","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Bear hunting is a practice that has been historically present in every culture in contact with the animal. Bears have been hunted since prehistoric times for their meat and fur. In addition to being a source of food, in modern times they have been favored by big game hunters due to their size and ferocity. Bear hunting has a vast history throughout Europe and North America, and hunting practices have varied based on location and type of bear."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bear-paw"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_paw"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","ref":"site/thewoksoflife-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","ref":"site/youtube-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true},{"name":"Red House Spice","ref":"site/redhousespice-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blog