dless (United States), Lady de Coverly (England), and oval-fruited Kishmish (Iran, Iraq, Palestine, Pakistan, Afghanistan, India). It is also known as a grape found in İzmir, or Manisa in Turkey, since this variety has been extensively grown in the region around those cities. It is assumed to originate from Asia Minor, which later became part of the Ottoman Empire."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sultana-grape"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultana_(grape)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Dundee cake","dish/dundee-cake"]]],["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine",[["Oliebol","dish/oliebol"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Currant","ingredient/currant"],["Seville orange","ingredient/seville-orange"],["Baking powder","ingredient/baking-powder"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Raisin","ingredient/raisin"],["Ribes","ingredient/ribes"],["Succade","ingredient/succade"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"],["Zest","ingredient/zest"]]}]},"ingredient/solanaceae":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/solanaceae","n":"Solanaceae","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Solanaceae (), commonly known as the nightshades, is a family of flowering plants in the order Solanales. The family contains approximately 2,700 species, several of which are used as agricultural crops, medicinal plants, and ornamental plants. Many members of the family have high alkaloid contents, making some highly toxic, but many—such as tomatoes, potatoes, eggplants and peppers—are commonly used in food around the world."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-solanaceae"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanaceae"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Karedok","dish/karedok"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Cucumber","ingredient/cucumber"],["Holy basil","ingredient/holy-basil"],["Kencur","ingredient/kencur"],["Krupuk","ingredient/krupuk"],["Mung bean sprout","ingredient/mung-bean-sprout"],["Pachyrhizus erosus","ingredient/pachyrhizus-erosus"],["Peanut sauce","ingredient/peanut-sauce"],["Shrimp paste","ingredient/shrimp-paste"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}]},"dish/kue-rangi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kue-rangi","n":"Kue rangi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kue rangi or also called sagu rangi is an Indonesian coconut kue or traditional snack made of a  coconut and starch-based batter and cooked in a special molded pan. It is one of the traditional Betawi snack of Jakarta. Kue rangi is often described as Indonesian coconut waffle."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kue-rangi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kue_rangi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}]},"dish/kusa-mochi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kusa-mochi","n":"Kusa mochi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kusa mochi, also known as yomogi mochi (蓬餅), is a Japanese confection. It is made from mochi and leaves of yomogi (Japanese mugwort). The leaves are kneaded into the mochi, giving it a vivid green color. The greenness depends on the amount of Japanese mugwort blended in the mochi."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kusa-mochi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kusa_mochi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Mochi","ingredient/mochi"],["Red bean paste","ingredient/red-bean-paste"],["Yomogi","ingredient/yomogi"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"